            <div xml:id="d839">

                <pb facs="0780" n="768" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg768"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 A.R./1072: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-15T17:00:00-04:00">May 15, 1940—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>94. Apropos the Argentine non-belligerency proposal, Foreign Minister has said to
                    newspaperman he cannot express an opinion now and that his attitude would be
                    influenced by attitude of Congress and by word from Washington for which he is
                    waiting.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
